1
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:07,400
Qingtian.

2
00:00:18,519 --> 00:00:21,760
I'll send you the footage for
Chunshan Su via cloud drive.

3
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:23,519
I've deleted everyone else's.

4
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:24,760
I only kept a copy for you.

5
00:00:25,879 --> 00:00:28,879
Thanks. I'll take off
right after the ceremony.

6
00:00:29,519 --> 00:00:31,280
Don't worry, I'm here.

7
00:00:32,280 --> 00:00:33,600
There's nothing to worry about.

8
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:36,080
Qingtian goes into the
mountains every year.

9
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:38,479
How long will it take to
shoot your documentary?

10
00:00:39,759 --> 00:00:41,879
Director Jiang said after
the spring tea season ends,

11
00:00:42,079 --> 00:00:44,079
we'll probably extend the
shoot for another month.

12
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:45,960
That'll be the end of May.

13
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,440
How long is your variety show shoot?

14
00:00:49,520 --> 00:00:50,560
About two months.

15
00:00:51,158 --> 00:00:52,519
It's alo at Tian Yi Lu.

16
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:55,320
I'll come hang out with
you when I have time.

17
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:07,500
"A Winter Sun Wakes the Wind in Spring Hills' Dream"

18
00:01:11,100 --> 00:01:14,800
(Episode 11: The very beginning)

19
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Pick one blind.

20
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:26,040
You just picked the
tea-colored one, didn't you?

21
00:01:26,760 --> 00:01:27,760
Mind your own business.

22
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:29,359
This blue bracelet suits you.

23
00:01:29,480 --> 00:01:30,680
Your name is Qinglang.

24
00:01:30,879 --> 00:01:32,480
A clear sky is blue.

25
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:35,359
Amo said this one
represents love. Wanna trade?

26
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:39,295
What does the tea-colored one represent?

27
00:01:39,319 --> 00:01:40,680
This one represents career.

28
00:01:40,799 --> 00:01:41,879
The color of the earth.

29
00:01:41,959 --> 00:01:43,519
It's the soil, the foundation.

30
00:01:44,799 --> 00:01:45,799
I'm leaving.

31
00:01:46,079 --> 00:01:47,079
Hey.

32
00:01:48,719 --> 00:01:50,039
Guess I don't have a choice then.

33
00:01:54,359 --> 00:01:56,719
Feng Qinglang is such a drama queen.

34
00:01:57,359 --> 00:01:58,359
It's pretty good.

35
00:02:00,185 --> 00:02:01,185
Brother Wenshu.

36
00:02:01,799 --> 00:02:03,560
If you make a move now,

37
00:02:03,599 --> 00:02:05,120
I'll still support you.

38
00:02:06,159 --> 00:02:09,159
Even though I think my brother
isn't good enough for you.

39
00:02:11,680 --> 00:02:13,120
Are you praising me,

40
00:02:13,479 --> 00:02:14,680
or putting down Changyang?

41
00:02:16,319 --> 00:02:19,400
There's no accounting for taste. Let's go.

42
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:28,560
When others went in,

43
00:02:29,159 --> 00:02:30,559
why didn't Amo give them bracelets?

44
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:34,759
Amo stared at me and said a
bunch of stuff. I didn't understand.

45
00:02:35,319 --> 00:02:37,680
But when Amo finally gave me the bracelet,

46
00:02:37,879 --> 00:02:39,520
I could feel his blessing.

47
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:41,719
He was probably welcoming you.

48
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,400
The elf prince of the tea mountain.

49
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:54,198
Brother Chu, just carry it upstairs.

50
00:02:54,199 --> 00:02:54,800
Okay.

51
00:02:54,801 --> 00:02:56,318
Director Jiang, you guys can
put the equipment in there.

52
00:02:56,319 --> 00:02:57,319
Okay, great.

53
00:02:57,560 --> 00:02:59,280
We have two bedrooms here.

54
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:01,319
We can clear out two more.

55
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:02,679
But they all have king-size beds.

56
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:03,680
No twin rooms.

57
00:03:03,719 --> 00:03:05,639
We need to figure out
the sleeping arrangements.

58
00:03:05,919 --> 00:03:07,399
You can stay at my master's place.

59
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:09,000
We can hold meetings on the first floor.

60
00:03:13,199 --> 00:03:14,759
Mr. Xu, should we bring the luggage in?

61
00:03:16,479 --> 00:03:17,120
Director Jiang.

62
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:17,599
Yes?

63
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:18,679
Is a king-size bed okay?

64
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:19,680
Oh, thank you, Mr. Xu.

65
00:03:19,719 --> 00:03:20,879
Whatever you arrange is fine.

66
00:03:26,893 --> 00:03:27,692
Qingtian.

67
00:03:27,716 --> 00:03:28,716
Yeah?

68
00:03:29,919 --> 00:03:31,360
You sort out the rooms.

69
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:33,560
If there's not enough space,

70
00:03:34,199 --> 00:03:36,119
I'll go find a bed and
breakfast in the village.

71
00:03:37,880 --> 00:03:39,119
A B&amp;B is too expensive.

72
00:03:41,879 --> 00:03:42,879
I've got money.

73
00:03:42,919 --> 00:03:44,158
Just because you have money
doesn't mean you can waste it.

74
00:03:44,159 --> 00:03:45,279
Spend it where it counts.

75
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:46,280
I'll go sort it out.

76
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:52,104
Brother Chu, can you share
a room with Director Jiang?

77
00:03:52,128 --> 00:03:52,929
He doesn't mind.

78
00:03:53,121 --> 00:03:54,158
Sure, why not?

79
00:03:54,159 --> 00:03:55,198
I'll go grab the luggage first.

80
00:03:55,199 --> 00:03:56,199
Okay.

81
00:03:56,879 --> 00:03:59,119
Brother Wenshu, you can
stay in Changyang's room.

82
00:03:59,120 --> 00:04:00,840
That way, no one else will touch his stuff.

83
00:04:01,159 --> 00:04:02,519
I'll go stay at my master's place.

84
00:04:02,919 --> 00:04:04,280
Your master's place is too far.

85
00:04:04,319 --> 00:04:06,135
It's too much of a hassle
going back and forth.

86
00:04:06,159 --> 00:04:08,680
If not, I'll go stay at Teacher Fu's place.

87
00:04:11,199 --> 00:04:12,478
You two should just share a room.

88
00:04:12,479 --> 00:04:14,520
I saw the bed, it's big
enough for both of you.

89
00:04:22,319 --> 00:04:24,519
Brother Wenshu, let me
help you hang up your clothes.

90
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:37,120
Qingtian.

91
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:38,120
Yeah?

92
00:04:38,519 --> 00:04:40,160
I'm a pretty quiet sleeper.

93
00:04:40,879 --> 00:04:42,600
But I'm not used to wearing a shirt to bed.

94
00:04:42,959 --> 00:04:45,079
So I didn't pack any.

95
00:04:45,560 --> 00:04:47,560
Let me see if there are
any in Changyang's closet.

96
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:50,519
- If you mind...
- I don't.

97
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:52,360
That's good.

98
00:04:54,319 --> 00:04:55,399
It's brand new.

99
00:04:57,360 --> 00:04:59,919
Mr. Xu, Director Jiang said we'll
have a meeting downstairs in a bit.

100
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:01,319
To finalize the shooting schedule.

101
00:05:02,319 --> 00:05:03,519
I'll sit this one out.

102
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:05,920
They'll feel uncomfortable if I'm there.

103
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:07,680
Qingtian.

104
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:10,160
You go have the meeting with the crew.

105
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:11,879
I'll get going then.

106
00:05:33,319 --> 00:05:35,839
I'll grab the shooting schedule.

107
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:47,759
Brother Wenshu, do you work out a lot?

108
00:05:48,360 --> 00:05:49,360
Yeah, I do.

109
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:50,759
I'm leaving now.

110
00:06:04,703 --> 00:06:06,576
[Changyang sent a picture of himself]

111
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:08,820
[Who do you want me
to send this too? Be direct]

112
00:06:08,830 --> 00:06:11,076
[I just want you to see, I sent
it to everyone in my family]

113
00:06:11,103 --> 00:06:12,816
[Look who became filial all of a sudden]

114
00:06:12,840 --> 00:06:14,520
[I'm going to train, can't talk]

115
00:06:16,603 --> 00:06:18,209
[He's sending the photo to Qinglang]

116
00:06:21,063 --> 00:06:23,529
[God of Wealth Xu: Let me
know if you've safely arrived]

117
00:07:47,736 --> 00:07:54,676
[Private message to Wajijilu: Send that
photo you took that night to Xu Changyang]

118
00:08:17,596 --> 00:08:21,096
[He saved the photo
to his camera roll]

119
00:10:36,639 --> 00:10:38,840
Hey Sister, Lang Di is back.

120
00:10:38,879 --> 00:10:41,639
But he said he doesn't want to
take any gigs before the variety show.

121
00:10:41,679 --> 00:10:42,959
None of them want to take gigs.

122
00:10:42,960 --> 00:10:44,480
Forcing me to make an appearance, huh?

123
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:52,320
What's going on with you?

124
00:10:53,519 --> 00:10:55,039
Brother Guo, let me ask you something.

125
00:10:55,440 --> 00:10:56,878
When we were on the Nanlou set,

126
00:10:56,879 --> 00:10:58,279
did you send me a message?

127
00:10:58,559 --> 00:10:59,559
The Nanlou set?

128
00:10:59,639 --> 00:11:00,639
What message?

129
00:11:04,159 --> 00:11:07,039
I wasn't acting well in that scene.

130
00:11:07,159 --> 00:11:08,679
The director gave me a lot of notes.

131
00:11:09,159 --> 00:11:11,439
Brother Guo, let me
borrow your phone for a sec.

132
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:13,416
I want to check the
behind-the-scenes footage we just shot.

133
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:15,559
If you want to see our Han Lu, just say so.

134
00:11:16,919 --> 00:11:17,919
Thanks, bro.

135
00:11:24,919 --> 00:11:27,360
Later, the director told me
to get ready for another take.

136
00:11:27,679 --> 00:11:29,639
That's when I got the message you sent me.

137
00:11:30,519 --> 00:11:31,639
Oh, this message.

138
00:11:31,759 --> 00:11:32,879
I sent it.

139
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:54,158
Sister, Sister, Sister! I finally
know why Han Lu refuses to

140
00:11:54,159 --> 00:11:55,878
do joint events with Qi Haoyu.

141
00:11:55,879 --> 00:11:56,360
Did you know?

142
00:11:56,360 --> 00:11:57,279
On the Nanlou set,

143
00:11:57,320 --> 00:11:58,959
Qi Haoyu actually used my phone to

144
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:00,720
send Han Lu a message cursing himself.

145
00:12:01,159 --> 00:12:02,918
That's how Han Lu found out about Qi Haoyu

146
00:12:02,919 --> 00:12:05,056
signing a performance-based
contract with the company.

147
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:05,879
Oh my god.

148
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:07,359
Just to get Han Lu into character,

149
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:08,960
he actually used such a dirty trick.

150
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:11,360
Using my phone to send him a message!

151
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:13,479
He probably thinks he's
so badass, doesn't he?

152
00:12:13,503 --> 00:12:15,061
The point is...

153
00:12:15,086 --> 00:12:17,080
Sis, why aren't you anxious at all?

154
00:12:18,879 --> 00:12:19,879
It's hot!

155
00:12:21,159 --> 00:12:22,840
When Han Lu asked if you sent it,

156
00:12:22,960 --> 00:12:24,080
what did you say?

157
00:12:25,639 --> 00:12:26,360
I'm just that good.

158
00:12:26,360 --> 00:12:27,360
I had a stroke of genius.

159
00:12:27,361 --> 00:12:28,758
I admitted it right on the spot.

160
00:12:28,759 --> 00:12:29,639
For the sake of the company's interests,

161
00:12:29,640 --> 00:12:31,159
I had to fall on my sword.

162
00:12:31,360 --> 00:12:34,039
If Qi Haoyu took the fall for this... Bah!

163
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:35,519
It was his mess to begin with!

164
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:37,239
But this matter absolutely cannot

165
00:12:37,240 --> 00:12:38,639
weigh on our Han Lu's mind.

166
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:40,038
Our Han Lu is just a kid.

167
00:12:40,039 --> 00:12:41,120
He's so innocent,

168
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:43,159
kind-hearted, and values relationships.

169
00:12:43,919 --> 00:12:45,678
I mean, even though it's not a huge deal,

170
00:12:45,679 --> 00:12:47,240
it's like a thorn.

171
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:50,879
It hurts so much to
pull it out of your heart.

172
00:12:53,279 --> 00:12:55,120
Hey Sister, how was my
performance just now?

173
00:12:55,159 --> 00:12:56,759
Did I look like a Best Actor?

174
00:12:57,360 --> 00:12:58,360
You fool.

175
00:12:58,919 --> 00:13:00,678
My crisis PR was so brilliant,

176
00:13:00,679 --> 00:13:01,679
how am I a fool?

177
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:06,039
Think about what Sister Lan would do.

178
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:24,720
Stop thinking about it, leave it to me.

179
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:26,439
You keep Lang Di in check for now.

180
00:13:26,440 --> 00:13:27,879
Let him get a good month's rest.

181
00:13:28,080 --> 00:13:30,679
The variety show with Shi
Yuhao was his own choice.

182
00:13:30,840 --> 00:13:31,840
I respect that.

183
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:33,678
You can tell him,

184
00:13:33,679 --> 00:13:34,519
if he regrets it,

185
00:13:34,519 --> 00:13:35,360
he can terminate the contract anytime.

186
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:36,679
The company has his back.

187
00:13:37,159 --> 00:13:40,120
Go on.

188
00:13:55,240 --> 00:13:56,678
You can't accept it right now.

189
00:13:56,679 --> 00:13:57,679
I totally understand.

190
00:13:58,159 --> 00:14:00,720
Because I was your age once too.

191
00:14:01,440 --> 00:14:03,759
If you don't want to attend
events, just take a breather.

192
00:14:04,279 --> 00:14:06,320
Look back on it when
you're in a better headspace.

193
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:08,360
I won't try to persuade you,

194
00:14:08,440 --> 00:14:10,120
and don't try to persuade yourself either.

195
00:14:10,440 --> 00:14:12,158
Whichever way your heart pulls you,

196
00:14:12,159 --> 00:14:13,320
just follow it.

197
00:14:29,826 --> 00:14:32,533
Lu, I wasn't the one who sent that message,

198
00:14:32,933 --> 00:14:35,700
I lied to you just to avoid
affecting your event with Haoyu.

199
00:14:36,786 --> 00:14:37,733
I'm sorry.

200
00:14:39,013 --> 00:14:42,459
Sister Lan just asked me to pass along
a message to you, I'll send it to you.

201
00:14:42,503 --> 00:14:44,183
[The message is the voiceover
that just played one minute earlier]

202
00:14:44,207 --> 00:14:46,293
Brother Guo, you don't need to say sorry.

203
00:14:46,843 --> 00:14:49,289
I believe the company gives me freedom and tolerance.

204
00:14:49,569 --> 00:14:51,403
I'll cooperate and
participate in the event.

205
00:14:58,080 --> 00:14:59,400
Asking you to let go of Changyang

206
00:14:59,840 --> 00:15:02,240
is probably harder than
finding a cure for regret, isn't it?

207
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:08,720
Leave it to time.

208
00:15:21,639 --> 00:15:23,480
The world is like a giant web.

209
00:15:24,440 --> 00:15:26,480
If I bounce on one spot,

210
00:15:27,519 --> 00:15:29,679
it sends ripples across the whole world.

211
00:15:32,679 --> 00:15:35,639
And then someone will fall
off because of those ripples.

212
00:15:38,720 --> 00:15:39,720
Mom.

213
00:15:40,720 --> 00:15:42,720
There are some things
I'll never dare to do again.

214
00:15:45,519 --> 00:15:47,839
If your mother from your
past three lives were still here,

215
00:15:48,445 --> 00:15:49,685
what would she say to you?

216
00:15:50,919 --> 00:15:52,679
"Brave" is the most hollow word.

217
00:15:52,919 --> 00:15:55,679
Many people are encouraged
to be brave their whole lives,

218
00:15:56,039 --> 00:15:58,199
but no one knows what
they're actually supposed to do.

219
00:15:58,919 --> 00:16:01,960
Because people think
bravery is about facing others,

220
00:16:02,440 --> 00:16:04,080
confessing to someone you like,

221
00:16:04,480 --> 00:16:06,240
or saying no to things you hate.

222
00:16:07,120 --> 00:16:08,120
In reality,

223
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:10,960
bravery just requires
facing yourself honestly.

224
00:16:11,679 --> 00:16:13,559
When you're terrified,
dare to admit your fear.

225
00:16:14,240 --> 00:16:15,919
When you love, dare to accept reality.

226
00:16:16,279 --> 00:16:17,360
That is bravery.

227
00:16:18,159 --> 00:16:20,199
Bravery isn't necessarily
forcing things to happen.

228
00:16:20,919 --> 00:16:22,879
It should be a vine that grows endlessly,

229
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:24,919
bearing abundant fruit,

230
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:27,440
growing without limits.

231
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:47,096
Tian, your tea-picking
skills are pretty good!

232
00:16:47,120 --> 00:16:49,038
I'm no good. Changyang is here.

233
00:16:49,039 --> 00:16:51,039
His tea-picking and
roasting skills are top-notch.

234
00:16:57,660 --> 00:16:59,540
Let's do an interview up there.

235
00:16:59,780 --> 00:17:00,780
Sure.

236
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:28,518
Tian, as a city kid,

237
00:17:28,519 --> 00:17:31,240
what made you suddenly want
to come to the tea mountains?

238
00:17:37,839 --> 00:17:40,440
I used to suffer from severe depression.

239
00:17:41,473 --> 00:17:43,753
By chance, I ended up here.

240
00:17:45,039 --> 00:17:48,440
When I stepped onto
the soil of the tea garden,

241
00:17:48,720 --> 00:17:52,919
I felt like all those drifting, unsettled
feelings finally grounded themselves.

242
00:17:53,279 --> 00:17:54,319
Standing here,

243
00:17:54,759 --> 00:17:56,680
I feel like a tea tree,

244
00:17:57,119 --> 00:17:58,880
growing solidly and steadily.

245
00:18:00,079 --> 00:18:01,880
I heard the locals say

246
00:18:02,039 --> 00:18:03,358
that however tall a tea
tree grows above ground,

247
00:18:03,359 --> 00:18:05,039
its roots grow just as deep below.

248
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:06,558
I finally understood.

249
00:18:06,559 --> 00:18:10,039
Human life doesn't just have one direction.

250
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:12,439
It can be like a tea tree,

251
00:18:12,440 --> 00:18:14,119
stretching in both directions,

252
00:18:14,440 --> 00:18:15,720
growing endlessly.

253
00:18:18,079 --> 00:18:19,079
Great. Cut!

254
00:18:26,119 --> 00:18:27,936
If Director Jiang's
questions are too sensitive,

255
00:18:27,960 --> 00:18:29,440
I'll tell him to avoid them.

256
00:18:30,119 --> 00:18:32,359
No need. I'll dodge whatever
I don't want to answer.

257
00:18:36,359 --> 00:18:37,279
Get some sleep.

258
00:18:37,279 --> 00:18:38,279
Yeah.

259
00:19:18,519 --> 00:19:19,680
Sharing a room?

260
00:19:20,039 --> 00:19:21,240
Absolutely not.

261
00:19:30,959 --> 00:19:31,599
Guo.

262
00:19:32,266 --> 00:19:32,679
Want a drink?

263
00:19:33,486 --> 00:19:34,653
I'm not thirsty. Thanks.

264
00:19:44,119 --> 00:19:45,119
Brother.

265
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:51,160
Why don't you deliver it yourself?

266
00:19:51,640 --> 00:19:53,839
Didn't you see he ignored me all day?

267
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:56,880
Did you do something guilty again?

268
00:19:57,480 --> 00:19:59,278
Brother, just knock on the door for me

269
00:19:59,279 --> 00:20:00,439
and give him the teapot.

270
00:20:00,440 --> 00:20:01,600
You don't have to say a word.

271
00:20:08,720 --> 00:20:09,720
Who is it?

272
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:10,880
Me.

273
00:20:14,119 --> 00:20:15,680
Brother, the teapot is yours.

274
00:20:18,519 --> 00:20:20,255
This teapot must be
pretty expensive, right?

275
00:20:20,279 --> 00:20:21,359
I've got money.

276
00:20:22,720 --> 00:20:24,360
When are you going to share some with me?

277
00:20:24,880 --> 00:20:26,039
You won the bet.

278
00:20:26,440 --> 00:20:28,040
You can buy as many teapots as you want.

279
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:31,559
How many teapots? Let me do the math.

280
00:20:34,319 --> 00:20:35,319
Qi Haoyu.

281
00:20:35,786 --> 00:20:37,826
Don't you think you're being nasty?

282
00:20:38,359 --> 00:20:39,480
Where is this coming from?

283
00:20:40,279 --> 00:20:42,136
Starting from when you refused
to cooperate with the event,

284
00:20:42,160 --> 00:20:43,680
the game had already begun, right?

285
00:20:43,920 --> 00:20:45,640
I was very cooperative.

286
00:20:46,759 --> 00:20:47,759
Qi Haoyu.

287
00:20:49,079 --> 00:20:50,839
Do you really take me for a fool?

288
00:20:53,519 --> 00:20:54,519
Cutting ties,

289
00:20:55,119 --> 00:20:56,359
ignoring messages,

290
00:20:57,759 --> 00:20:58,759
asking to be scolded,

291
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:02,480
then flipping the script and
pretending to realize your mistakes,

292
00:21:03,640 --> 00:21:05,079
using me to create trending topics.

293
00:21:06,119 --> 00:21:07,240
Before the trending topics,

294
00:21:07,359 --> 00:21:09,479
you gambled with the company magazine.

295
00:21:12,519 --> 00:21:13,519
Qi Haoyu.

296
00:21:14,319 --> 00:21:16,079
You had a lot of fun
playing me, didn't you?

297
00:21:17,160 --> 00:21:21,101
Even when acting, you had to use
Brother Guo's phone to text and provoke me.

298
00:21:23,279 --> 00:21:24,480
From beginning to end,

299
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:26,519
what exactly am I to you?

300
00:21:27,839 --> 00:21:28,839
A tool?

301
00:21:29,359 --> 00:21:30,359
Just a tool,

302
00:21:31,319 --> 00:21:32,225
not even a person?

303
00:21:32,249 --> 00:21:33,249
Hey.

304
00:21:37,079 --> 00:21:38,519
You're overthinking this.

305
00:21:38,759 --> 00:21:40,759
I was just thinking about our future.

306
00:21:40,952 --> 00:21:41,513
We can make money

307
00:21:41,641 --> 00:21:43,321
and break free from the company's control.

308
00:21:43,420 --> 00:21:44,420
How awesome is that?

309
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:47,640
Hey, don't you think this is
just like us acting in a movie?

310
00:21:47,839 --> 00:21:49,078
It's also because the character
Ran Qi was written so well.

311
00:21:49,079 --> 00:21:50,519
I learned a lot from him.

312
00:21:51,680 --> 00:21:53,319
Alright.

313
00:21:54,473 --> 00:21:55,273
Stop being mad.

314
00:21:55,297 --> 00:21:57,097
I'll take you out for
some good food tonight.

315
00:21:58,440 --> 00:22:00,279
You're really proud of what you've done.

316
00:22:01,559 --> 00:22:03,959
One magazine bet is enough
to feed us for a lifetime.

317
00:22:03,960 --> 00:22:05,960
Did I ever say I wanted
to spend my life with you?

318
00:22:08,519 --> 00:22:09,359
You're a sitting duck.

319
00:22:09,480 --> 00:22:11,279
You're the duck! Get lost!

320
00:22:12,640 --> 00:22:14,400
Let go of me!

321
00:22:25,960 --> 00:22:27,600
You still want to create trending topics?

322
00:22:27,960 --> 00:22:29,360
Make a bet with me first.

323
00:22:30,400 --> 00:22:34,799
If there can only be exploitation
and profit between us,

324
00:22:35,559 --> 00:22:37,159
then let's keep it purely transactional.

325
00:22:37,799 --> 00:22:39,759
Put the profit-sharing
ratio in the contract.

326
00:23:27,039 --> 00:23:28,039
Qinglang.

327
00:23:31,552 --> 00:23:34,953
Qinglang.

328
00:23:49,993 --> 00:23:50,993
Qinglang.

329
00:24:22,160 --> 00:24:24,680
If I said I regretted it now,

330
00:24:26,279 --> 00:24:27,959
you definitely wouldn't believe me, right?

331
00:24:33,559 --> 00:24:36,439
Then did you think I recorded this
variety show just to make a comeback?

332
00:24:42,680 --> 00:24:52,821
Actually, I just wanted to leave my failed past
with a few memories I still dare to look back on.

333
00:24:56,200 --> 00:24:58,000
Changyang.

334
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:20,759
Do you remember that year after we wrapped
up filming and went our separate ways home?

335
00:25:21,200 --> 00:25:22,639
It snowed at my place,

336
00:25:22,640 --> 00:25:24,000
but it didn't at yours.

337
00:25:24,880 --> 00:25:27,400
Then you told me you really loved snow,

338
00:25:28,000 --> 00:25:29,400
so I took pictures of it for you.

339
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:36,558
Back then, we would talk on the phone

340
00:25:36,559 --> 00:25:38,159
for four or five hours every day,

341
00:25:38,160 --> 00:25:39,359
until you fell asleep.

342
00:25:45,160 --> 00:25:47,320
At that time, you didn't
even know I had a girlfriend.

343
00:25:49,599 --> 00:25:51,400
Actually, I was pretty conflicted too.

344
00:25:55,839 --> 00:25:57,680
Remember what I told you back then?

345
00:25:58,279 --> 00:26:04,000
I said if you suddenly
disappeared right then,

346
00:26:04,680 --> 00:26:07,080
I would never be able to
forget you for the rest of my life.

347
00:26:10,279 --> 00:26:11,559
Pretty childish, right?

348
00:26:14,960 --> 00:26:16,760
I couldn't see clearly
who I loved back then,

349
00:26:18,000 --> 00:26:22,960
so I liked using death
to rank the people I loved.

350
00:26:35,880 --> 00:26:38,160
Actually, I've always been pretty insecure.

351
00:26:42,599 --> 00:26:46,759
But I've always, always been
incredibly confident about you.

352
00:26:46,799 --> 00:26:49,400
Because I know all too well how
deeply you value relationships.

353
00:26:53,200 --> 00:26:54,960
I always felt that

354
00:26:58,839 --> 00:27:01,279
no matter how high or far you flew,

355
00:27:02,799 --> 00:27:04,960
I would always be number one in your heart.

356
00:27:12,160 --> 00:27:13,160
But I

357
00:27:18,480 --> 00:27:20,799
never expected that this number one spot

358
00:27:25,799 --> 00:27:27,400
would be taken by someone else.

359
00:27:29,680 --> 00:27:30,680
Yeah.

360
00:27:39,680 --> 00:27:40,999
If I died in front of you right now,

361
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:44,440
you wouldn't even care, would you?

362
00:28:25,400 --> 00:28:27,079
Brother Guo wants one from this angle.

363
00:28:27,200 --> 00:28:28,640
Alright, I'll take a couple.

364
00:28:30,680 --> 00:28:32,400
Hey, look here, looking good.

365
00:28:33,033 --> 00:28:34,232
What do you think?

366
00:28:34,400 --> 00:28:35,400
Touch it up for me.

367
00:28:35,680 --> 00:28:36,680
Sure.

368
00:28:42,359 --> 00:28:44,759
You seem to be in a good mood lately.

369
00:28:45,640 --> 00:28:48,359
Of course. Dumping someone
can piss them off to death.

370
00:28:48,759 --> 00:28:51,199
I don't get it. This angle
of yours is pretty good.

371
00:28:51,200 --> 00:28:51,559
Okay.

372
00:28:51,559 --> 00:28:52,559
Come on.

373
00:29:01,119 --> 00:29:02,119
Hi.

374
00:29:02,400 --> 00:29:04,278
Mind if we get to know
each other and add...

375
00:29:04,279 --> 00:29:06,039
I'm his manager. Add me instead.

376
00:29:06,160 --> 00:29:07,279
You're a celebrity?

377
00:29:07,799 --> 00:29:09,359
You don't follow celebrities, do you?

378
00:29:09,579 --> 00:29:10,699
I'm following [chasing after] one right now.

379
00:29:12,152 --> 00:29:13,392
Hey, how about...

380
00:29:14,240 --> 00:29:15,240
Ah, sure.

381
00:29:18,240 --> 00:29:18,799
Thanks.

382
00:29:18,799 --> 00:29:19,799
No problem.

383
00:29:30,640 --> 00:29:33,118
Mr. Jin, it's my first time
meeting an investor like you.

384
00:29:33,119 --> 00:29:34,239
You don't look at the pitch deck,

385
00:29:34,240 --> 00:29:35,400
you don't look at the script.

386
00:29:35,552 --> 00:29:38,153
I thought I had found myself in
the middle of a short drama story.

387
00:29:39,279 --> 00:29:41,839
To be honest, money like yours,

388
00:29:41,880 --> 00:29:43,119
we don't dare to accept.

389
00:29:45,079 --> 00:29:46,880
Afraid it's dirty money?

390
00:29:47,920 --> 00:29:49,240
It goes against investment logic.

391
00:29:49,480 --> 00:29:50,640
When we do projects,

392
00:29:50,759 --> 00:29:52,440
we don't just take any kind of money.

393
00:29:52,519 --> 00:29:55,079
Ah, of course, I'm not saying
there's a problem with your money.

394
00:29:56,240 --> 00:29:58,480
Then we can interact more.

395
00:29:58,680 --> 00:30:00,480
I was too reckless today.

396
00:30:10,079 --> 00:30:11,079
My daughter...

397
00:30:27,640 --> 00:30:29,680
Brother, is your variety show over?

398
00:30:30,480 --> 00:30:32,480
Should I take the house back?

399
00:30:32,880 --> 00:30:34,279
Where does it say it's your house?

400
00:30:34,839 --> 00:30:36,519
If I've lived in it, it's mine.

401
00:30:43,720 --> 00:30:44,960
You guys aren't filming today?

402
00:30:45,960 --> 00:30:47,856
Director Jiang took the
crew to shoot some B-roll.

403
00:30:47,880 --> 00:30:50,640
If you hadn't come, we'd be changing
locations this afternoon anyway.

404
00:30:51,839 --> 00:30:54,160
Boss Xu even knows professional jargon now.

405
00:30:55,640 --> 00:30:59,240
Brother, why has your tone changed since
you finished recording the variety show?

406
00:31:00,039 --> 00:31:01,039
What tone?

407
00:31:02,519 --> 00:31:03,680
You sound so aggressive.

408
00:31:04,480 --> 00:31:06,119
Did Shi Yuhao feed you gunpowder?

409
00:31:07,279 --> 00:31:09,359
It's alright. I'm not
particularly uncomfortable.

410
00:31:09,960 --> 00:31:11,319
Where's your next stop?

411
00:31:11,559 --> 00:31:13,960
We're heading deeper
into Molie. Are you coming?

412
00:31:14,359 --> 00:31:16,480
No, I'll stay right here.

413
00:31:18,240 --> 00:31:19,839
Are you not working after this?

414
00:31:20,559 --> 00:31:21,640
I can push work back.

415
00:31:22,160 --> 00:31:24,078
Anyway, I have Boss Xu backing me up.

416
00:31:24,079 --> 00:31:25,240
I'm not short on money.

417
00:31:25,680 --> 00:31:27,720
Brew some tea. I'm thirsty.

418
00:31:33,480 --> 00:31:34,815
If you hadn't mentioned the variety show,

419
00:31:34,839 --> 00:31:36,118
I would've thought you
took a role in a short drama,

420
00:31:36,119 --> 00:31:37,119
playing a little punk.

421
00:31:39,240 --> 00:31:40,760
You're going to live here by yourself?

422
00:31:42,680 --> 00:31:43,896
Never mind, pretend I didn't ask.

423
00:31:43,920 --> 00:31:45,680
Brother Wenshu, we're
going to buy supplies.

424
00:31:47,640 --> 00:31:48,440
What do you want to eat?

425
00:31:48,441 --> 00:31:49,561
We'll bring it back for you.

426
00:31:53,119 --> 00:31:54,319
Enough rations for seven days.

427
00:31:54,519 --> 00:31:57,015
If you want to freeload, go to
Master's house and find his wife.

428
00:31:57,039 --> 00:32:00,119
Or look for Xiao Hei, Azha, or Azha's wife.

429
00:32:02,079 --> 00:32:03,240
You know them all anyway.

430
00:32:04,119 --> 00:32:06,279
You won't starve to death staying in Molie.

431
00:32:06,559 --> 00:32:07,919
We're done packing, we're leaving!

432
00:32:14,640 --> 00:32:15,920
I want to eat bamboo worms.

433
00:35:09,463 --> 00:35:11,256
[He's calling Qingtian]

434
00:35:13,236 --> 00:35:16,323
[generic "Can't Connect" message]

435
00:35:42,159 --> 00:35:43,159
Which one do you choose?

436
00:35:43,519 --> 00:35:44,519
I want both.

437
00:35:44,679 --> 00:35:45,760
You can only choose one.

438
00:37:51,719 --> 00:37:52,719
Azha.

439
00:37:53,159 --> 00:37:54,439
Hey, the big star has arrived.

440
00:37:54,440 --> 00:37:55,440
When did you get back?

441
00:37:55,840 --> 00:37:56,840
Yesterday.

442
00:37:57,159 --> 00:37:58,159
Sprained your ankle?

443
00:37:58,480 --> 00:37:59,480
Yeah.

444
00:38:00,039 --> 00:38:01,639
I wanted to ask if you have any tea oil.

445
00:38:01,679 --> 00:38:03,159
I ran out of the stuff I had at home.

446
00:38:03,239 --> 00:38:06,280
Yes, I'll call Ali later and have
her bring some over to you.

447
00:38:06,440 --> 00:38:07,719
Just wait at home.

448
00:38:08,079 --> 00:38:09,320
Okay, thanks, Azha.

449
00:38:10,880 --> 00:38:11,880
Working hard?

450
00:38:12,280 --> 00:38:13,959
Man, the work never ends.

451
00:38:13,960 --> 00:38:16,879
Some kid knocked down a
whole patch of my bamboo.

452
00:38:16,880 --> 00:38:18,480
I have to go back and clean it up later.

453
00:38:28,719 --> 00:38:30,039
Running so fast with a bum leg.

454
00:40:55,676 --> 00:40:58,036
"Those who can see, know."

455
00:41:01,670 --> 00:41:02,936
[He's posting his one foot on Weibo]

456
00:41:04,029 --> 00:41:07,356
[Various fan accounts responding with names
referencing his relationship to Changyang]

457
00:41:08,840 --> 00:41:10,079
They're all fakes.

458
00:41:25,449 --> 00:41:27,783
[Brother Guo is calling]

459
00:41:34,840 --> 00:41:37,320
Lang Di, please come back soon.

460
00:41:37,440 --> 00:41:39,760
Look at the mess you're living in.

461
00:41:40,039 --> 00:41:41,679
How did you hurt your foot again?

462
00:41:41,719 --> 00:41:42,639
You can't even take care of yourself.

463
00:41:42,640 --> 00:41:44,440
Just sit tight and let someone wait on you.

464
00:41:44,559 --> 00:41:45,559
I'm not going back.

465
00:41:46,589 --> 00:41:48,389
[God of Wealth Xu is calling]

466
00:41:53,440 --> 00:41:55,560
I'll have Secretary Chu go
over and take care of you.

467
00:41:56,440 --> 00:41:57,440
No need.

468
00:41:58,450 --> 00:42:00,123
[Xu Changyang [with
his nickname] is calling]

469
00:42:02,159 --> 00:42:04,320
I said no need, really.

470
00:42:05,683 --> 00:42:07,510
[Shi Yuhao is calling]

471
00:42:22,159 --> 00:42:23,320
Will you be okay on your own?

472
00:42:25,473 --> 00:42:27,313
Am I completely useless in your eyes?

473
00:42:27,760 --> 00:42:28,840
Other than acting?

474
00:42:30,480 --> 00:42:31,320
I should probably go over there.

475
00:42:31,321 --> 00:42:32,681
Or you can come back to Shangjing.

476
00:42:32,760 --> 00:42:34,519
I won't bother you.

477
00:42:34,719 --> 00:42:35,719
Shi Yuhao.

478
00:42:36,159 --> 00:42:39,439
Don't think we're best buddies just because
we shot a variety show for two months.

479
00:42:40,239 --> 00:42:41,718
Don't forget what happened
seven years ago at that...

480
00:42:41,719 --> 00:42:43,960
fan meeting, how you
grabbed me by the collar.

481
00:42:44,360 --> 00:42:46,239
How you deliberately provoked me on stage.

482
00:42:46,280 --> 00:42:48,719
And how you schemed to steal my fans.

483
00:42:48,960 --> 00:42:50,296
And now you're trying to cling to me again.

484
00:42:50,320 --> 00:42:51,880
Have you no shame? Get lost.

485
00:42:58,336 --> 00:43:00,576
[Zoom in on the crazy
nickname for Xu Changyang]

486
00:43:18,159 --> 00:43:20,038
Did Changyang leave his phone at home?

487
00:43:20,039 --> 00:43:21,079
It's with his sister.

488
00:43:21,360 --> 00:43:24,440
That can't be, he posted
that photo himself last time.

489
00:43:25,280 --> 00:43:26,719
Could he have it on him?

490
00:43:26,960 --> 00:43:29,440
Technically, phones aren't
allowed during training.

491
00:43:35,119 --> 00:43:39,280
Sorry, the subscriber you dialed
cannot be connected for the moment.

492
00:43:39,519 --> 00:43:41,159
Please redial later.

493
00:43:41,679 --> 00:43:43,679
Sorry, the subscriber you dialed...

494
00:44:01,800 --> 00:44:04,000
Our Jialan Shanying isn't
exactly a big company.

495
00:44:04,159 --> 00:44:05,639
We only handle small projects.

496
00:44:05,679 --> 00:44:07,638
Mr. Jin, your vibe really
matches our company.

497
00:44:07,639 --> 00:44:09,239
I'm truly very happy about that.

498
00:44:09,440 --> 00:44:11,158
But as for the artists in our company...

499
00:44:11,159 --> 00:44:12,159
I don't call the shots.

500
00:44:12,199 --> 00:44:13,518
They have their own ideas.

501
00:44:13,519 --> 00:44:14,800
And their own autonomy.

502
00:44:15,119 --> 00:44:16,760
You can't force a good fit.

503
00:44:18,039 --> 00:44:19,759
Boss Fang, don't be in such a rush.

504
00:44:19,760 --> 00:44:21,160
We have plenty of time ahead of us.

505
00:44:42,639 --> 00:44:43,639
My eldest grandson!

506
00:44:44,199 --> 00:44:46,320
Look, is it pretty?

507
00:44:49,159 --> 00:44:50,159
Grandma.

508
00:44:50,639 --> 00:44:52,159
I hurt my foot.

509
00:44:52,760 --> 00:44:54,559
Ah, what did you say?

510
00:44:55,840 --> 00:44:56,840
It's pretty.

511
00:44:57,119 --> 00:44:59,639
Guess who bought this for Grandma?

512
00:45:00,159 --> 00:45:01,719
It was Junjun!

513
00:45:02,159 --> 00:45:04,239
Junjun ordered it for Grandma from abroad.

514
00:45:04,559 --> 00:45:06,319
It took over two months
to arrive in the mail.

515
00:45:06,320 --> 00:45:10,320
That lousy post office even
sent it to the wrong place at first.

516
00:45:10,440 --> 00:45:13,000
Yesterday, I called Junjun...

517
00:45:13,360 --> 00:45:15,840
To check the tracking number,
and they finally found it today.

518
00:45:15,920 --> 00:45:17,440
Isn't it just gorgeous?

519
00:45:17,840 --> 00:45:18,840
Grandma.

520
00:45:19,039 --> 00:45:21,159
What time did you call Junjun yesterday?

521
00:45:21,559 --> 00:45:24,360
In the evening. Anyway, I gotta go.

522
00:45:24,559 --> 00:45:26,718
Grandma's going to dance in the square.

523
00:45:26,719 --> 00:45:27,719
Hey.

524
00:45:45,960 --> 00:45:47,558
I told you to come over, but you wouldn't.

525
00:45:47,559 --> 00:45:48,999
Now I have to go through
the trouble of bringing it to you.

526
00:45:49,000 --> 00:45:50,800
Come over for a meal
tomorrow. Here, take it.

527
00:45:52,039 --> 00:45:53,039
Thanks, Azha.

528
00:48:34,360 --> 00:48:35,960
My distant tea mountain...

529
00:48:36,360 --> 00:48:38,559
Gazes at his ocean from
thousands of miles away.

530
00:48:41,360 --> 00:48:43,215
When the termite mushroom
breaks through the soil...

531
00:48:43,239 --> 00:48:45,559
the mountain's delicacies
can rival any seafood.

532
00:48:55,360 --> 00:48:56,920
The subscriber has hung up.

533
00:48:57,039 --> 00:48:58,840
Please leave a message after the beep.

534
00:49:05,159 --> 00:49:07,638
A human mother saved her child...

535
00:49:07,639 --> 00:49:09,239
From the jaws of a tiger cub.

536
00:49:10,000 --> 00:49:11,920
She was hailed by humans as a great mother.

537
00:49:13,039 --> 00:49:15,760
But the tiger cub lost its food and died.

538
00:49:16,920 --> 00:49:19,599
Every act of protection is
rooted in one's own perspective.

539
00:49:19,719 --> 00:49:21,896
Judgments of right and wrong
are merely differences in stance.

540
00:49:21,920 --> 00:49:25,920
But a great mother still
commands awe and respect.

541
00:49:27,039 --> 00:49:28,039
Namaste.

542
00:49:49,000 --> 00:49:50,800
You can use ruthless methods.

543
00:49:51,119 --> 00:49:53,719
But did you get my permission
before using my knife?

544
00:49:54,400 --> 00:49:57,495
Sister Lan kept that video on her cloud
drive for seven years without posting it.

545
00:49:57,518 --> 00:49:59,183
If she really didn't want to post it.
Why didn't she delete it?

546
00:50:00,119 --> 00:50:01,119
You're very rational.

547
00:50:02,239 --> 00:50:03,639
So rational that it scares me.

548
00:50:05,360 --> 00:50:07,080
No matter how justified your reasons are...

549
00:50:07,599 --> 00:50:09,159
You casually fired a shot...

550
00:50:09,400 --> 00:50:10,960
And killed the person closest to me.

551
00:50:11,159 --> 00:50:12,199
Calm down.

552
00:50:15,519 --> 00:50:17,760
He fulfilled his childhood wish.

553
00:50:18,199 --> 00:50:20,679
Starting from when he
met the one he loved at 16...

554
00:50:20,920 --> 00:50:23,679
All the way to 26, 36...

555
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:26,000
And finally to 116.

556
00:50:26,559 --> 00:50:27,559
A hundred years.

557
00:50:27,800 --> 00:50:31,280
Spending a hundred springs, summers, autumns,
and winters in this world with his lover.

558
00:50:31,400 --> 00:50:33,518
That's a happiness
worthy of the history books.

559
00:50:33,519 --> 00:50:34,519
By his calculations...

560
00:50:34,719 --> 00:50:36,440
I'll have to live to be 118.

561
00:52:15,000 --> 00:52:16,000
A ghost!

562
00:52:19,400 --> 00:52:20,400
A ghost!

563
00:54:04,559 --> 00:54:06,039
Whose ghost husband has returned?

564
00:54:13,239 --> 00:54:14,239
You lying ghost.

565
00:54:17,593 --> 00:54:20,553
Do you think I'd believe it just because
you took a photo with my brother?

566
00:54:21,239 --> 00:54:22,239
Xu Changyang.

567
00:54:23,800 --> 00:54:24,960
I told you before.

568
00:54:26,000 --> 00:54:27,120
Let's go back to square one.

569
00:54:29,960 --> 00:54:30,960
Yeah.

570
00:54:31,239 --> 00:54:32,239
I'm back.

